#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# frobenius_number

#% text
# `frobenius_number(coins)` gives the largest integer that cannot be written as a non-negative combination of the positive integers `coins` (`inf` when their gcd exceeds 1).

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
frobenius_number([3, 5])
#% output
#= 7

#% cell
frobenius_number([6, 9, 20])
#% output
#= 43

#% cell
frobenius_number([4, 6])
#% output
#= inf

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `frobenius_solve`, `gcd`
